.nh
.TH "PB-COMPLETION-POWERSHELL" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-completion-powershell - Generate the autocompletion script for powershell


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb completion powershell [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Generate the autocompletion script for powershell.

.PP
To load completions in your current shell session:

.EX
pb completion powershell | Out-String | Invoke-Expression
.EE

.PP
To load completions for every new session, add the output of the above command
to your powershell profile.

.PP
This command does not support --json output; it rejects that mode before execution. Use --help --json for structured command help.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for powershell

.PP
\fB--no-descriptions\fP[=false]
	disable completion descriptions


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-completion(1)\fP
